# A `params: [...]` frontmatter key (kexhq/kex#171 M3) fixes the generated
# function's parameter names, order, AND types explicitly, overriding
# free-variable inference — the same list `Template.scan`'s own
# `Parsed#parameters` already parses (kexhq/kex#252, M1). The body's own
# reading order is `count` then `title`; the frontmatter declares the
# opposite, and the call below only works in the FRONTMATTER's order —
# proving that order won, not inference's first-appearance one. `count`'s
# declared `: Integer` is enforced too: swap the call's arguments and it is
# a compile-time type mismatch, not a runtime surprise.

main do
  let show = Template.text(`---
params: [title, count: Integer]
---
<%= count %> of <%= title %>`)
  IO.printLine(show("Items", 3))
end
